description.p:
Fluoropolymers made by the process of this invention can also contain units derived from monomers that introduce functional groups into the polymer to modify surface characteristics, to provide cross-linking sites, and the like. Functional monomers that introduce pendant side groups having such functionality can have the general formula 

 wherein each Y is independently H, F or Cl, and Z contains a functional group. Preferably, each Y is F and -Z is -Rf-X, wherein Rf is a fluorinated diradical and X is a functional group 

that may contain CH2 groups. Examples of such functional monomers include bromotetrafluorobutene. Examples of functional monomers also include fluorovinylethers such as CF2=CF[OCF2CF(CF3)]m-O-(CF2)nCH2OH as disclosed in U.S. Patent 4,982,009 and the alcoholic ester CF2=CF[OCF2CF(CF3)]m-O-(CF2)n-(CH2)p-O-COR as disclosed in U.S. Patent 5,310,838. Additional fluorovinylethers include CF2=CF[OCF2CF(CF3)]mO(CF2)nCOOH and its carboxylic ester CF2=CF[OCF2CF(CF3)]mO(CF2)nCOOR disclosed in U.S. Patent 4,138,426. In these formulae, m = 0-3, n = 1-4, p = 1-2 and R is methyl or ethyl. Preferred such fluorovinylethers include CF2=CF-O-CF2CF2-SO2F;
